/* book exam traps: N1 is fan speed; the start schedule runs on N2, the HP spool. | A hot start is an EGT exceedance; a hung start is N2 stopping below idle after light-off; a wet start has no light-off at all. | Cut-out is triggered by N2, not by clock time, and it comes well above self-sustaining speed. | Early or excess fuel causes a hot start. Ignition must be on before fuel, so early ignition is correct, not a fault. | Spark energy goes with V², not V: doubling the capacitor voltage gives four times the energy. */
